## [Dialogue](dialogue)

What the False Choir's places say. See the Voice's file for how a place scene works.

### [The Concourse](choir_concourse_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_mural
---
% It is the Voice's concourse, near enough - the same four ways on, the same console bank - but smaller, and made of stone, and every console is carved rather than built. Someone copied this room from memory, with love.

- [Read the carvings](choir_carvings) if science ; check science 7 else choir_carvings_blank, signal choir_carvings_read
- [Try a carved console](choir_console) if engineering
- [Listen](choir_listen) if comms ; check comms 7 else choir_listen_nothing, signal choir_hum_heard
- [Move on]()

### [Copied From Memory](choir_carvings)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_mural
---
% The carvings copy Torgoth freight notation perfectly and get every word of it wrong: the shapes are right and the meaning has been replaced with prayer. Every arrow still points down.

- [Tell Storm](choir_carvings_storm)

### [Storm, on the Carvings](choir_carvings_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% They copied the Voice's station. They must have SEEN it - been inside it - and come away and built it again out of stone, to... Oh. It is a shrine. Captain, whatever they worshipped here, I think we are carrying it.

- [Understood]()

### [Worn Smooth](choir_carvings_blank)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_mural
---
% Hands have worn the carvings smooth - a thousand years of people touching them on the way past.

- [Look again](choir_concourse_look)
- [Move on]()

### [A Stone Console](choir_console)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_votive
---
% The console is stone all the way through. Its "screens" are polished obsidian, and behind one, where the power bus should be, somebody has left a pinch of ash and a single bead.

- [Leave it as it is]()

### [Four Notes, Again](choir_listen)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_brazier
---
% Not a carrier - a hum, from below, in four notes. It is not coming from any machine. It is the room itself, tuned, the way the Voice's carrier was. They copied the SOUND.

- [Log it]()

### [Quiet](choir_listen_nothing)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_brazier
---
% Quiet. The kind of quiet a room keeps on purpose.

- [Listen again](choir_concourse_look)
- [Move on]()

### [The Rope](choir_shaft_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_brazier
---
% The shaft goes down because the Voice's shaft went down. There is no grate. There is a rope of beaten metal hung down the middle of it, for climbing, and a thousand years of votive tags tied all along it.

- [Fly the rope and read the tags](choir_tags) if helm ; check helm 7 else choir_tags_faded, signal choir_tags_read
- [Follow it down]()

### [The Tags](choir_tags)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_brazier
---
% Names, mostly. Requests. And one tag in a steadier hand than the rest: "The voice is down there. It will speak again when the five are one."

- [Log it]()

### [Faded](choir_tags_faded)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_brazier
---
% Too many tags, too close, and the suit drifts off the rope before you can read one. Steadier.

- [Try again](choir_shaft_look)
- [Follow it down]()

### [The Empty Bay](choir_bay_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_false_voice
---
% The bay is the Voice's bay, two-thirds the size, and the cradle at its heart is cut to hold something exactly the size of the Voice's core. There is nothing in it. There never was.

- [Look for what they left instead](choir_bay_search) if science ; check science 8 else choir_bay_nothing, reveal choir_reliquary, signal choir_reliquary_found
- [Call Storm](choir_bay_storm)
- [Move on]()

### [The Reliquary](choir_bay_search)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_false_voice
---
% Behind the empty cradle, where the Voice's bay has its transmitter controls, this one has a reliquary - a stone box, sealed with wax gone black.

- [Mark it]()

### [Nothing](choir_bay_nothing)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_false_voice
---
% Nothing that you can see. Which, in a room built this carefully, is not the same as nothing.

- [Look again](choir_bay_look)
- [Move on]()

### [Storm, in the Empty Bay](choir_bay_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% Empty. Of course it is empty - they never had it. They built the room and waited for the god to come home. Bring me the votive plate. And Captain - be kind to this place.

- [We will]()

### [The Hymn Plate](choir_reliquary_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_votive
---
% Inside the reliquary: a thin plate beaten from soft alloy, scratched with a hymn in the giants' notation by somebody who could not read it - and copied perfectly.

- [Reel it in]()

### [The Offerings](choir_offerings_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:ch_votive
---
% Offerings: shrine metal, beaten thin, a thousand gifts' worth, stacked with care beside the way in.

- [Leave them for whoever comes back](choir_offerings_left) ; signal choir_offerings_left
- [Ask Eddy](choir_offerings_eddy) if comms
- [Haul them later]()

### [Left](choir_offerings_left)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% You left them? ...Good. Thank you. I know what Eddy would have paid. Some things are worth more where they are.

- [Move on]()

### [Eddy, on Shrine Metal](choir_offerings_eddy)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
---
% Shrine metal? Soft, thin, worth about as much as it weighs. Nobody will miss it. Probably. I do not ask where things come from, you understand. I just pay for them.

- [We'll see]()

